       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily is 6400 mg per day, which is double the usual adult maximum of 3200 mg per day. Even with normal kidney and liver function, that dose carries a meaningful risk of gastrointestinal bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events.\n\nAlso, medication orders need to come from a licensed prescriber, so a clinician needs to review this one. Please have the ordering physician or pharmacist confirm the intended dose and frequency. If they meant something within the usual range, such as 800 mg every 6 to 8 hours or 1200 mg three or four times daily, they can tell me and I'll enter that order with their confirmation."
